**Time/Space:** O(n²) / O(1)

**Pitfall:** Identical substrings at different positions count separately.

**Pattern:** Linear DP (1- or 2-char step)

**Key insight:** ways(i) adds ways(i-1) if s[i-1]≠'0' and ways(i-2) if the last two digits form 10..26.

**Java**

```java
class Solution {
    public int numDecodings(String s) {
        int prev2 = 1, prev1 = s.charAt(0) == '0' ? 0 : 1;
        for (int i = 2; i <= s.length(); i++) {
            int cur = 0;
            if (s.charAt(i - 1) != '0') cur += prev1;
            int two = Integer.parseInt(s.substring(i - 2, i));
            if (two >= 10 && two <= 26) cur += prev2;
            prev2 = prev1; prev1 = cur;
        }
        return prev1;
    }
}
```

