**Time/Space:** O(amount · coins) / O(amount)

**Pitfall:** Greedy largest-coin-first is wrong for coin sets like [1,3,4], amount 6.

**Pattern:** Kadane variant tracking min and max

**Key insight:** A negative number swaps the roles of the running max and min, so keep both.

**Java**

```java
class Solution {
    public int maxProduct(int[] nums) {
        int hi = nums[0], lo = nums[0], best = nums[0];
        for (int i = 1; i < nums.length; i++) {
            int x = nums[i];
            if (x < 0) { int t = hi; hi = lo; lo = t; }
            hi = Math.max(x, hi * x);
            lo = Math.min(x, lo * x);
            best = Math.max(best, hi);
        }
        return best;
    }
}
```

**Python**

```python
