class Solution:
    def maxProduct(self, nums: List[int]) -> int:
        hi = lo = best = nums[0]
        for x in nums[1:]:
            if x < 0:
                hi, lo = lo, hi
            hi = max(x, hi * x)
            lo = min(x, lo * x)
            best = max(best, hi)
        return best
```

**Time/Space:** O(n) / O(1)

**Pitfall:** Tracking only the max loses the big negative that a later negative flips positive.

**Pattern:** Prefix DP

**Key insight:** ok[i] is true if some j<i has ok[j] and s[j..i) in the dictionary.

**Java**

```java
class Solution {
    public boolean wordBreak(String s, List<String> wordDict) {
        Set<String> dict = new HashSet<>(wordDict);
        boolean[] ok = new boolean[s.length() + 1];
        ok[0] = true;
        for (int i = 1; i <= s.length(); i++)
            for (int j = 0; j < i && !ok[i]; j++)
                ok[i] = ok[j] && dict.contains(s.substring(j, i));
        return ok[s.length()];
    }
}
```

**Python**

