**Time/Space:** O(n) / O(1)

**Pitfall:** Zeros are only fatal if no earlier index can jump over them.

**Pattern:** Greedy BFS by levels

**Key insight:** Each jump covers a window; the next window ends at the farthest reach from the current one.

**Java**

```java
class Solution {
    public int jump(int[] nums) {
        int jumps = 0, end = 0, far = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < nums.length - 1; i++) {
            far = Math.max(far, i + nums[i]);
            if (i == end) { jumps++; end = far; }
        }
        return jumps;
    }
}
```

