class Solution:
    def jump(self, nums: List[int]) -> int:
        jumps = end = far = 0
        for i in range(len(nums) - 1):
            far = max(far, i + nums[i])
            if i == end:
                jumps += 1
                end = far
        return jumps
```

**Time/Space:** O(n) / O(1)

**Pitfall:** Looping to the last index adds an extra jump when you're already there.

**Pattern:** Greedy reset

**Key insight:** If total gas ≥ total cost a start exists; when the tank goes negative, the start must be after the current station.

**Java**

```java
class Solution {
    public int canCompleteCircuit(int[] gas, int[] cost) {
        int total = 0, tank = 0, start = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < gas.length; i++) {
            int d = gas[i] - cost[i];
            total += d;
            tank += d;
            if (tank < 0) { tank = 0; start = i + 1; }
        }
        return total < 0 ? -1 : start;
    }
}
```

**Python**

```python
from typing import List

class Solution:
    def canCompleteCircuit(self, gas: List[int], cost: List[int]) -> int:
        total = tank = start = 0
        for i, (g, c) in enumerate(zip(gas, cost)):
            total += g - c
            tank += g - c
            if tank < 0:
                tank, start = 0, i + 1
        return -1 if total < 0 else start
```

**Time/Space:** O(n) / O(1)

**Pitfall:** Simulating from every start is O(n²) and unnecessary.

**Pattern:** Greedy from smallest (sorted counts)

**Key insight:** The smallest remaining card must start a group; consume its run.

**Java**

```java
class Solution {
    public boolean isNStraightHand(int[] hand, int groupSize) {
        if (hand.length % groupSize != 0) return false;
        TreeMap<Integer, Integer> cnt = new TreeMap<>();
        for (int c : hand) cnt.merge(c, 1, Integer::sum);
        while (!cnt.isEmpty()) {
            int first = cnt.firstKey();
            for (int v = first; v < first + groupSize; v++) {
                Integer k = cnt.get(v);
                if (k == null) return false;
                if (k == 1) cnt.remove(v); else cnt.put(v, k - 1);
            }
        }
        return true;
    }
}
```

**Python**

```python
from collections import Counter
from typing import List

class Solution:
    def isNStraightHand(self, hand: List[int], groupSize: int) -> bool:
        if len(hand) % groupSize:
            return False
        cnt = Counter(hand)
        for first in sorted(cnt):
            k = cnt[first]
            if k == 0:
                continue
            for v in range(first, first + groupSize):
                if cnt[v] < k:
                    return False
                cnt[v] -= k
        return True
```

**Time/Space:** O(n log n) / O(n)

**Pitfall:** Starting groups from an arbitrary card instead of the minimum can fail valid hands.

**Pattern:** Greedy filter

**Key insight:** Ignore any triplet exceeding target in some slot; the rest are safe — check they cover each target value.

**Java**

```java
class Solution {
    public boolean mergeTriplets(int[][] triplets, int[] target) {
        boolean[] hit = new boolean[3];
        for (int[] t : triplets) {
            if (t[0] > target[0] || t[1] > target[1] || t[2] > target[2]) continue;
            for (int i = 0; i < 3; i++) if (t[i] == target[i]) hit[i] = true;
        }
        return hit[0] && hit[1] && hit[2];
    }
}
```

**Python**

