**Time/Space:** O(n) / O(1)

**Pitfall:** Using a triplet with any overshooting value poisons the result forever (max never decreases).

**Pattern:** Greedy with last-occurrence

**Key insight:** Extend the current part to the last occurrence of every char seen; cut when i reaches that end.

**Java**

```java
class Solution {
    public List<Integer> partitionLabels(String s) {
        int[] last = new int[26];
        for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++) last[s.charAt(i) - 'a'] = i;
        List<Integer> res = new ArrayList<>();
        int start = 0, end = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++) {
            end = Math.max(end, last[s.charAt(i) - 'a']);
            if (i == end) { res.add(end - start + 1); start = i + 1; }
        }
        return res;
    }
}
```

