**Pattern:** Shrinking boundaries

**Key insight:** Walk top row, right column, bottom row, left column, then shrink; guard the last two for single rows/cols.

**Java**

```java
class Solution {
    public List<Integer> spiralOrder(int[][] m) {
        List<Integer> res = new ArrayList<>();
        int top = 0, bot = m.length - 1, left = 0, right = m[0].length - 1;
        while (top <= bot && left <= right) {
            for (int c = left; c <= right; c++) res.add(m[top][c]);
            for (int r = top + 1; r <= bot; r++) res.add(m[r][right]);
            if (top < bot) for (int c = right - 1; c >= left; c--) res.add(m[bot][c]);
            if (left < right) for (int r = bot - 1; r > top; r--) res.add(m[r][left]);
            top++; bot--; left++; right--;
        }
        return res;
    }
}
```

