**Pattern:** Grade-school multiplication

**Key insight:** Digit i × digit j lands at positions i+j and i+j+1 of a result array.

**Java**

```java
class Solution {
    public String multiply(String a, String b) {
        int[] pos = new int[a.length() + b.length()];
        for (int i = a.length() - 1; i >= 0; i--)
            for (int j = b.length() - 1; j >= 0; j--) {
                int sum = (a.charAt(i) - '0') * (b.charAt(j) - '0') + pos[i + j + 1];
                pos[i + j + 1] = sum % 10;
                pos[i + j] += sum / 10;
            }
        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();
        for (int d : pos) if (!(sb.length() == 0 && d == 0)) sb.append(d);
        return sb.length() == 0 ? "0" : sb.toString();
    }
}
```

